{
  "name": "security-hygiene",
  "version": "5.0.0",
  "schema": "houserules/pack@1.2.0",
  "topics": {
    "security-hygiene": {
      "title": "Dependency, commit, and test hygiene"
    }
  },
  "areas": {
    "global": {
      "paths": []
    }
  },
  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "security-hygiene.exact-pins",
      "kind": "rule",
      "area": "global",
      "standing": true,
      "summary": "Pin exact versions. Install only with a CLI (`pnpm add --save-exact`, `cargo add <crate>@=<version>`). Never write a version number by hand.",
      "body": [
        "Ranges (`^`, `~`) widen the attack surface. Resolve to the latest stable version at install time.",
        "The deterministic check covers `package.json` and `Cargo.toml`; ranges inside the `engines` object are floors, not dependency pins, and are exempt. In `Cargo.toml` it misses a table header with inner spaces (`[ dependencies ]`) and a dotted key (`serde.version = \"1\"`). Other ecosystems and the missed forms are judged by the reviewer under the same rule."
      ],
      "tags": [
        "dependencies",
        "supply-chain"
      ],
      "source": {
        "date": "2026-08-30",
        "by": "docs",
        "ref": "houserules seed"
      },
      "check": {
        "type": "grep-absent",
        "level": "fail",
        "files": [
          "**/package.json",
          "**/Cargo.toml"
        ],
        "flags": "m",
        "pattern": "\"(?=(?:[\\^~]|>=?|<=?)\\s*\\d|\\*\"|latest\"|\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)*\\.x\")(?<!\"engines\":\\s*\\{[^}]*)|^(?=[ \\t]*(?:\"[^\"\\n]+\"|[A-Za-z0-9_-]+)[ \\t]*=[ \\t]*(?:[\"']\\d|\\{[^}\\n]*\\bversion[ \\t]*=[ \\t]*[\"']\\d))(?<=^[ \\t]*\\[(?:[^\\]\\n]*\\.)?(?:dev-|build-)?dependencies\\][ \\t]*(?:#[^\\n]*)?\\r?\\n(?:(?![ \\t]*\\[)[^\\n]*\\n)*?)[ \\t]*(?:\"[^\"\\n]+\"|[A-Za-z0-9_-]+)|^(?=[ \\t]*version[ \\t]*=[ \\t]*[\"']\\d)(?<=^[ \\t]*\\[(?:[^\\]\\n]*\\.)?(?:dev-|build-)?dependencies\\.[^\\]\\n]+\\][ \\t]*(?:#[^\\n]*)?\\r?\\n(?:(?![ \\t]*\\[)[^\\n]*\\n)*?)[ \\t]*version",
        "scope": "changed"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "security-hygiene.tool-pins-are-exact",
      "kind": "rule",
      "area": "global",
      "summary": "Pin each tool of a mise `[tools]` table to a full version; a channel, a prefix, or a range admits an unvetted release.",
      "body": [
        "A channel (`latest`, `stable`, `lts`) follows new releases, and `system` takes whatever release the PATH holds. A prefix (`22`, `0.18`, `prefix:1.22`) matches the newest release of a line. A range (`~`, `^`, `<`, `>`, `=`, `*`) matches many releases. Each one installs a release that nobody vetted. Write the full version, for example `22.1.0`.",
        "The check reads the `[tools]` table of each mise config file, a plain value or the `version` of an inline table. It misses a `[tools.<name>]` table, a version array, and the `ref:`, `path:`, and `sub-<n>:` prefixes. The reviewer judges those under the same rule."
      ],
      "tags": [
        "dependencies",
        "supply-chain"
      ],
      "source": {
        "date": "2026-10-22",
        "by": "docs",
        "ref": "HR-214"
      },
      "check": {
        "type": "grep-absent",
        "level": "fail",
        "files": [
          "**/mise.toml",
          "**/.mise.toml",
          "**/.mise.*.toml",
          "**/mise.*.toml",
          "**/mise/config.toml",
          "**/mise/config.*.toml",
          "**/mise/conf.d/**/*.toml",
          "**/.mise/config.toml",
          "**/.mise/config.*.toml",
          "**/.mise/conf.d/**/*.toml",
          "**/.config/mise.toml",
          "**/.config/mise/*.toml",
          "**/.config/mise/conf.d/**/*.toml"
        ],
        "flags": "m",
        "pattern": "^(?=[ \\t]*(?:\"[^\"\\n]+\"|[A-Za-z0-9_.:@/-]+)[ \\t]*=[ \\t]*(?:[\"'](?:latest|lts[^\"']*|stable|nightly|beta|system|prefix:[^\"']*|\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?|[~^<>=*][^\"']*)[\"']|\\{[^}\\n]*\\bversion[ \\t]*=[ \\t]*[\"'](?:latest|lts[^\"']*|stable|nightly|beta|system|prefix:[^\"']*|\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?|[~^<>=*][^\"']*)[\"']))(?<=^[ \\t]*\\[tools\\][ \\t]*(?:#[^\\n]*)?\\r?\\n(?:(?![ \\t]*\\[)[^\\n]*\\n)*?)[ \\t]*(?:\"[^\"\\n]+\"|[A-Za-z0-9_.:@/-]+)",
        "scope": "changed"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "security-hygiene.tool-versions-pins-are-exact",
      "kind": "rule",
      "area": "global",
      "summary": "Pin each tool of a `.tool-versions` file to a full version; a channel, a prefix, or a range admits an unvetted release.",
      "body": [
        "A line of a `.tool-versions` file names a tool and a version. A channel (`latest`, `stable`, `lts`), `system` (whatever release the PATH holds), a bare major or major.minor, a `prefix:` value, or a range (`~`, `^`, `<`, `>`, `=`, `*`) admits a release that nobody vetted. Write the full version, for example `node 22.1.0`.",
        "The check reads the first version of a line, with or without a trailing comment. It misses a line with a second version. The reviewer judges that line under the same rule."
      ],
      "tags": [
        "dependencies",
        "supply-chain"
      ],
      "source": {
        "date": "2026-10-22",
        "by": "docs",
        "ref": "HR-214"
      },
      "check": {
        "type": "grep-absent",
        "level": "fail",
        "files": [
          "**/.tool-versions"
        ],
        "flags": "m",
        "pattern": "^[^#\\s]\\S*[ \\t]+(?:latest|lts\\S*|stable|nightly|beta|system|prefix:\\S*|\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?|[~^<>=*]\\S*)[ \\t]*(?:#[^\\n]*)?\\r?$",
        "scope": "changed"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "security-hygiene.dependency-vetting",
      "kind": "rule",
      "area": "global",
      "standing": true,
      "summary": "Verify every new dependency is well-maintained before adding it. Record the check in the task report's `dependency_vetting` field.",
      "body": [
        "Check recent releases, commit activity, and issue responsiveness.",
        "Outdated, stale, or abandoned dependencies are a no-go."
      ],
      "tags": [
        "dependencies",
        "supply-chain"
      ],
      "source": {
        "date": "2026-08-30",
        "by": "docs",
        "ref": "houserules seed"
      },
      "check": {
        "type": "report-field",
        "level": "fail",
        "if": [
          "**/package.json",
          "package-lock.json",
          "pnpm-lock.yaml",
          "pnpm-workspace.yaml",
          "yarn.lock",
          "**/Cargo.toml",
          "Cargo.lock",
          "**/pyproject.toml",
          "**/requirements*.txt",
          "uv.lock",
          "go.mod",
          "go.sum",
          "**/Gemfile",
          "Gemfile.lock",
          "**/composer.json",
          "composer.lock",
          "**/mise.toml",
          "**/.mise.toml",
          "**/.mise.*.toml",
          "**/mise.*.toml",
          "**/.tool-versions",
          "**/mise/config.toml",
          "**/mise/config.*.toml",
          "**/mise/conf.d/**/*.toml",
          "**/.mise/config.toml",
          "**/.mise/config.*.toml",
          "**/.mise/conf.d/**/*.toml",
          "**/.config/mise.toml",
          "**/.config/mise/*.toml",
          "**/.config/mise/conf.d/**/*.toml"
        ],
        "field": "dependency_vetting"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "security-hygiene.no-focused-tests",
      "kind": "rule",
      "area": "global",
      "standing": true,
      "summary": "Never commit a focused test (`.only(`).",
      "body": [],
      "tags": [
        "testing"
      ],
      "source": {
        "date": "2026-08-30",
        "by": "docs",
        "ref": "houserules seed"
      },
      "check": {
        "type": "grep-absent",
        "level": "fail",
        "files": [
          "**/*.test.ts",
          "**/*.test.tsx",
          "**/*.test.js",
          "**/*.test.jsx",
          "**/*.test.mjs",
          "**/*.spec.ts",
          "**/*.spec.tsx",
          "**/*.spec.js",
          "**/*.spec.mjs"
        ],
        "pattern": "\\.only\\(",
        "scope": "changed"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "security-hygiene.verify-current-docs",
      "kind": "rule",
      "area": "global",
      "standing": true,
      "summary": "Verify every library, tool, and framework API against current docs before use. Internal knowledge is stale.",
      "body": [
        "Use a docs source that is current (a docs MCP such as context7 when available, or the official documentation site). Record what you verified in the report's `docs_verified`."
      ],
      "tags": [
        "docs",
        "dependencies"
      ],
      "source": {
        "date": "2026-08-30",
        "by": "docs",
        "ref": "houserules seed"
      },
      "check": {
        "type": "report-field",
        "level": "warn",
        "if": [
          "**/*.mjs",
          "**/*.mts",
          "**/*.ts",
          "**/*.tsx",
          "**/*.js",
          "**/*.jsx",
          "**/*.rs",
          "**/*.py",
          "**/*.go",
          "**/*.rb",
          "**/package.json",
          "**/Cargo.toml",
          "**/pyproject.toml",
          "go.mod"
        ],
        "field": "docs_verified",
        "non_empty": true
      }
    }
  ]
}
